WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.980
In this video, you insert an ISO image into the CD-ROM drive of a running virtual machine and eject it again, without restarting the virtual machine.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.620
The virtual machine demo-cdrom is running. Open it.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.540
Select the Volumes tab.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:24.490
Below the root disk, the virtual machine has a CD-ROM drive on the SATA bus. It shows No media.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.400
Select Insert Image.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.620
Keep the drive name, cdrom, and choose the Alpine Linux ISO image.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.640
Select Apply.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:45.570
The drive now holds the Alpine ISO image. It was attached live, and the virtual machine is still running.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.090
When you no longer need the media, select Eject Image.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.970
Confirm that you want to eject the image from the cdrom drive.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:01.500
The drive shows No media again. The drive itself stays in place, ready for the next image.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.350
Throughout both changes, the virtual machine kept running.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:16.260
You inserted and ejected an ISO image while the virtual machine kept running. Next, you work with volume snapshots and images.
